  §5A Story About You!§r
§6╚════════◦♣◦═╝
§8This is a story 
about you. 

In the realm of Craftadia, where ancient whispered secrets and moonlit nights hold an eerie allure, there resided an individual. You possessed a very§r 
#- §8skeptical mind, immune to the tales of magic and curses that plagued the pages of Witch-Craft Magazine. 

Despite the warnings and chilling stories, you scoffed at the nonsense and believed the magazine was nothing more than a collection of fanciful fiction.§r
#- §8You settled down to read a particularly spine-tingling issue of the magazine. The §4𝕳𝖆𝖑𝖑𝖔𝖜𝖊𝖊𝖓 𝕰𝖉𝖎𝖙𝖎𝖔𝖓§8, always 
a treat, or maybe a trick. As you delved into the pages, you laughed with amusement, each word only serving to reinforce the insanity of it's author. This was meant to be a
#- §8random 'fake article' that makes the magazine have a reason to call itself a magazine, not some random story about you. Why would it be? It’s not like you are important. You are not the hero of this story. You are the victim. Unbeknownst to you, the very act of reading this story§r
#- §8had woven an insidious spell, one that thrived on your doubt and disbelief. 

With each passing sentence, an invisible thread of magic wound itself around your consciousness...

tugging at the 
edges of your 
reality.§r
#- §8As the story progressed, the atmosphere in the room you’re currently in grew increasingly oppressive. Out the corner of your eyes you think you can see something watching. 

The air grew thick with an unsettling energy. 

Yet, you keep reading.§r
#- §8You are certain that this was just an attempt to spook you. 

Did your screen 
just flicker?

A subtle change 
crept over you. 
Your skepticism wavered, and a chill slithered down your spine. A whisper of doubt wormed it's way§r 
#- §8into your thoughts, planting seeds of uncertainty. 

The words on the paGe sEemed To bLur and tWist, takiNg on A lifE of tHeIr oWn as they seeped into your mind. 

Unease settled upon you, and you tried to shake it off...§r 
#- §8The air a little colder.
Was that a bug you felt crawling on your face just now?§r

§7You don’t hear the deathly scream of Sweetpea through your screen behind the static.§r 

§8You tried to tear 
your gaze away 
from this story...§r
#- §8But you still turned to this next page as your eyes remained locked as if held by an invisible force. 

A sense of impending doom is in the air like a heavy fog. Your room fades away, and you find yourself here, inside a twisted dreamscape. Trapped inside my story.§r 
#- §5ɨȶ reachedӜ out with ghostlyӜ fingersӜ andӜ consumedӜ you. 

§8↑That happened in the spaces between the words you just read↑ 
I’m done saving people. Save yourself. 
After all, this §owas§r 
§8a story about§r §7you.§r
