#- §a╔═◦🧪◦════════╗§r
    §2I Need A Doctor!§r
§a╚════════◦🧪◦═╝§r
§2In a desolate corner of a toxic island, now cloaked in perpetual gloom, a sinister tale of magic vs science was about to unfold. 
A witch whose name once evoked warmth and kindness, had transformed into a vessel...§r 
#- §2of malevolence. Her anger was a tempest, and her heart, once gentle, had grown twisted. 

Dr. Link, a brilliant but sometimes morally compromised scientist, bore the weight of guilt. She had known the risks when she embarked on the ill-fated quest to§r
#- §2separate Sweetpea from §5ɨȶ.§2 

Even though it worked, the consequences far outweighed what both Dr. Link and Sweetpea had bargained for. But Links obsession with unraveling the mysteries of §5ɨȶ §2had led her down a path she was about to regret.
#- §2Deep within the heart of her laboratory, a cold, sterile place filled with mechanical wonders and cold steel, Dr. Link sought refuge from the witch she had broken. She had withdrawn, using technology as a means of escape. 
She had barricaded herself within her lab, her gaze fixated on§r 
#- §2the array of computer monitors, graphs and data, a feeble attempt to distract herself.

As she tinkered with her machines, the doctor’s heart clenched with remorse. 

“An accident,” she whispered to herself,§r
#- §2“I never meant for that to happen.” 
But outside her mechanical fortress, 
Sweetpea watched... 
Her presence grew stronger with each passing day.  

Lights from monitors and screens 
filtered through the laboratory’s shiny corridors...§r
#- §2Sweetpea wandered into the laboratory. Her once-bright eyes were now dark voids, her echoes of laughter sent shivers down Dr. Link’s spine.
In her head she heard Sweetpea’s voice. “§6Accident or not§2,” Sweetpea hissed, “§6you created a monster§2.” Dr. Link, overwhelmed by fear,
#- §2could only watch as her laboratory’s machines hummed to life on their own. Every monitor flashing images of Sweetpea’s traumatic experience inside the lab.§r

§7Link couldn’t hear 
the deathly scream of Sweetpea through 
the screens behind the static.§r
#- §2“§6You can’t escape§2” Sweetpea taunted. 
Dr. Link, now trapped in a digital cocoon, watched as Sweetpea seized control of her beloved laboratory. 
Lines of code danced across the screens; §70010110§2. Unique_bot aka Bestie Bot, ran into the room to try stop her, but with a snap of her fingers,
#- §2Bot shut down instantly. Test Subject Pete was soon after only to be met with a flick of a wrist and then unconsciousness. 

Every single lab creature, like The Giant Plant and The Warden, let out a booming sound of distress.§r
#- §2Dr. Link stammered, her voice trembling like the leaves in a storm. “You asked for my help, you wanted §5ɨȶ§2 gone, YOU did this too yourself.” Broken glassware and shattered equipment lay scattered across the floor. “§6You are right… but YOU could have stopped... 
and you didn’t§2”.
#- §2Everything went calm. Softness fell upon Sweetpea's face. "§6You hurt me Link, I wanted to hurt you§2". A pile of read Witch-Craft Magazines lay on the floor beside Link. Sweetpea carefully picked up the books and put them back neatly. "I do care, you know" spoke Link like a friend. "§6I know§2"...
