#- §5ₜwₒ wₒᵣdₛ: ₐᵤₜₒₘₐₜᵢc wᵣᵢₜᵢₙg!§r
§6Hey, now that's 
not a bad idea. 
Get myself into a trance/dream-like state, let my subconscious mind take the wheel! We could get so much information that way, from the other side. The veil is thin this time of year...
LET'S DO THIS!! §r✍
#- §2In the depths of an ancient forest, there lived a powerful witch named Marigold, her eyes as deep and dark as the secrets she held. With every lifetime she lived, she carried the memories of her past selves...

An endless burden that weighed heavily on her immortal soul. 
#- §2The one desire that eluded her across the eons was the simple joy of motherhood.

Determined to fill the void in her heart, Marigold delved into forbidden arts, merging nature's essence with dark magic to create life anew. 
#- §2With her arcane knowledge, she concocted a spell of petals and shadows, birthing the Flower Maidens. ❀ 

These ethereal beings, with bodies made of delicate petals, leaves and eyes as bright as the moon, were the witches greatest creation.
#- §2Yet, every time a Flower Maiden came 
to life, a part of their soul was devoured by §0The Darkness§2, a force that hungered for the very essence of existence. For Life! 
As the Flower Maidens danced and blossomed among the moonlit glades, the witch observed them with bittersweet pride,
#- §2for she knew the cost of her creation.

One fateful night, a deep, sinister voice echoed through the woods, the voice of §0The Darkness§2. None had ever heard it speak before. It demanded more, its hunger insatiable 
and its power 
growing stronger. 
#- §2Marigold realised the grave mistake she had made. 

Her beautiful creations had become instruments for more destruction, unwillingly feeding §0The Darkness §2that continued to consume each world and force Craftadia to begin again, and again, and again...
#- §2Haunted with grief and pain, she decided to undo all her creations. 

With each death, the forest mourned, its trees weeping leaves of sorrow. 

The Flower Maidens, innocent and pure, were sacrificed one by one. Children.
#- §2In a final, heartbreaking act, Marigold channeled her most powerful magic to sever the connection between the Flower Maidens and §0The Darkness§2.

As the dark force recoiled, the last remaining Maidens crumbled into petals, their essence, dust.
#- §2The witch, fell into eternal grief, forever mourning the loss of her children. The tale of Marigold and her Flower Maidens faded into myth. 

Until many lives later, when the lonely witch decided; maybe just one more? And so The 'Last' Flower Maiden's story began... 
#- 


§2“Nature is not human-hearted, but then Fern took her first breath...”§r 

